Ambassador Jennifer Locetta
Alternative Representative for Special Political Affairs
New York, New York
AS DELIVERED
Thank you, Mr. President, and thank you to our briefers.
The Houthis escalated their destabilizing activity in the region by launching missile and drone attacks against Israel on at least six occasions, most recently on April 4. They have made common cause with the Islamic Republic of Iran and acted in support of its violations of international law.
The Houthis’ willingness to drag Yemen into conflict for the sake of its benefactors in Tehran is the latest demonstration of its total disregard for the people of Yemen.
Inside Yemen, the Houthis continue to detain, attack, and terrorize their fellow Yemenis. On March 16, the Houthis launched a missile strike against Yemeni families gathered for an Iftar meal, killing ten people, including six children. This was preceded by the forced disappearance of several Sunni Imams, part of a larger pattern of Houthi repression of Sunni religious practices.
Moreover, the Houthis have unjustly detained more than 70 UN staff, along with humanitarian workers and other staff of civil society organizations and diplomatic missions, including the U.S. Mission. We call for their immediate and unconditional release.
The Iranian regime has long enabled the Houthis’ destabilizing activities through the supply of arms and related materiel and logistical and intelligence support. This is in clear defiance of this Council’s resolutions.
We call on all vessels bound for Houthi-controlled ports to comply with the UN Verification and Inspection Mechanism (UNVIM) requirements, as the Republic of Yemen Ministry of Transportation has reiterated to international shipping companies and port authorities.
Colleagues, Resolution 2817 represented the international community’s consensus that we cannot sit idly by as the Iranian regime and its proxies and partners undermine regional and international stability. All Member States must abide by resolutions to deprive the Houthis of the resources needed for their destabilizing activities.
Thank you.
