Ambassador Tammy Bruce
Deputy Representative of the United States to the United Nations
New York, New York
AS DELIVERED
Thank you, Mr. President. And thanks also to Assistant Secretary-General Khiari for your briefing. And of course, a special thank you to High Representative Kallas, for your briefing.
The European Union can and should play an important role in international peace and security—in Europe and beyond—and we welcome UN-EU cooperation to that end.
To play that meaningful role, the UN and the EU should focus on their foundational purposes and avoid burdensome policies that stifle free speech or innovation or infringe on national decision-making.
America wants a strong Europe as it means a more stable and prosperous world.
For that reason, we call on our European partners to step up, increase defense spending, and shoulder greater responsibility for their own security. This will also assist the EU to make choices allowing them to make a serious difference for the Europe and the world.
President Trump works constantly to end conflicts and never-ending wars across the globe. As he has noted, he could do this by himself, but he shouldn’t have to.
With our shared goal to strengthen European defense capabilities, we also ask the EU to expand, not impede, cooperation on transatlantic defense industrial bases and roll back protectionist barriers. These barriers pose risks to collective deterrence and will only slow down European rearmament.
As Europe takes ownership of its security, the United States will continue to push for a negotiated and durable end to the Russia-Ukraine war. This barbaric war and its death and devastation must stop now.
Thank you.
